# The European Economy

```elixir
Mix.install([
  # To try a local checkout use {:eurostatx, path: Path.join(__DIR__, "..")} instead
  {:eurostatx, "~> 0.1"},
  {:kino_explorer, "~> 0.1"},
  {:kino_vega_lite, "~> 0.1"}
])
```

## Introduction

A tour of the European economy with three key indicators: inflation, unemployment and GDP growth,
plus a look at regional disparities.

```elixir
alias Explorer.DataFrame, as: DF
alias Explorer.Series
alias VegaLite, as: Vl

require Explorer.DataFrame

countries = ~w(DE FR IT ES NL BE PL SE AT PT IE GR)
```

## Inflation

The annual rate of change of the HICP, for every month since 2021, as a heatmap:

```elixir
inflation =
  Eurostatx.Statistics.data_as_data_frame!("prc_hicp_minr",
    filters: [geo: ["EA" | countries], unit: "RCH_A", coicop18: "TOTAL"],
    start_period: "2021-01",
    labels: true
  )

Vl.new(width: 700, height: 320, title: "HICP - annual rate of change (%)")
|> Vl.data_from_values(DF.select(inflation, ["time", "geo_label", "value"]))
|> Vl.mark(:rect)
|> Vl.encode_field(:x, "time", type: :ordinal, title: nil, axis: [label_angle: -90])
|> Vl.encode_field(:y, "geo_label", type: :nominal, title: nil)
|> Vl.encode_field(:color, "value", type: :quantitative, scale: [scheme: :redyellowblue, reverse: true, domain_mid: 2])
```

Which countries had the highest inflation in the last month?

```elixir
latest = inflation |> DF.pull("date") |> Series.max()

inflation
|> DF.filter(date == ^latest)
|> DF.sort_by(desc: value)
|> DF.select(["geo_label", "time", "value", "flag"])
```

## Unemployment

The seasonally adjusted unemployment rate, for the total population and for young people:

```elixir
unemployment =
  Eurostatx.Data.get_as_data_frame!("une_rt_m",
    filters: [geo: ["EU27_2020", "ES", "DE", "FR", "IT"], age: ["TOTAL", "Y_LT25"], sex: "T", unit: "PC_ACT", s_adj: "SA"],
    start_period: "2015-01",
    labels: true
  )

Vl.new(width: 300, height: 250)
|> Vl.data_from_values(DF.select(unemployment, ["date", "geo_label", "age_label", "value"]))
|> Vl.mark(:line)
|> Vl.encode_field(:x, "date", type: :temporal, title: nil)
|> Vl.encode_field(:y, "value", type: :quantitative, title: "% of the labour force")
|> Vl.encode_field(:color, "geo_label", type: :nominal, title: nil)
|> Vl.encode_field(:column, "age_label", type: :nominal, title: nil)
```

## GDP Growth

The quarterly growth of the GDP in volume (chain linked volumes, percentage change on the previous
period, seasonally and calendar adjusted), from the SDMX API in wide shape:

```elixir
gdp =
  Eurostatx.Data.get_as_data_frame!("namq_10_gdp",
    filters: [geo: ["EU27_2020", "DE", "FR", "IT", "ES"], unit: "CLV_PCH_PRE", s_adj: "SCA", na_item: "B1GQ"],
    start_period: "2022-Q1",
    shape: :wide
  )
```

```elixir
long = Eurostatx.Data.get_as_data_frame!("namq_10_gdp",
  filters: [geo: ["EU27_2020", "DE", "FR", "IT", "ES"], unit: "CLV_PCH_PRE", s_adj: "SCA", na_item: "B1GQ"],
  start_period: "2022-Q1"
)

Vl.new(width: 700, height: 300, title: "GDP - growth on the previous quarter (%)")
|> Vl.data_from_values(DF.select(long, ["time", "geo", "value"]))
|> Vl.mark(:bar)
|> Vl.encode_field(:x, "time", type: :ordinal, title: nil)
|> Vl.encode_field(:x_offset, "geo", type: :nominal)
|> Vl.encode_field(:y, "value", type: :quantitative, title: "%")
|> Vl.encode_field(:color, "geo", type: :nominal, title: nil)
```

## Regional Disparities

The GDP per inhabitant in purchasing power standards (PPS) of the NUTS 2 regions, relative to the EU
average. The ten richest and poorest regions:

```elixir
regions =
  Eurostatx.Statistics.data_as_data_frame!("nama_10r_2gdp",
    filters: [unit: "PPS_EU27_2020_HAB"],
    geo_level: :nuts2,
    last_periods: 1,
    labels: true
  )
  |> DF.filter(not is_nil(value))

eu_average =
  Eurostatx.Statistics.data_as_data_frame!("nama_10r_2gdp",
    filters: [unit: "PPS_EU27_2020_HAB", geo: "EU27_2020"],
    last_periods: 1
  )
  |> DF.pull("value")
  |> Series.first()

regions = DF.mutate(regions, index: round(value / ^eu_average * 100, 0))

DF.concat_rows(
  regions |> DF.sort_by(desc: value) |> DF.head(10),
  regions |> DF.sort_by(asc: value) |> DF.head(10)
)
|> DF.select(["geo", "geo_label", "time", "value", "index"])
```

The distribution of the regions of each of the largest countries (the first two letters of a NUTS
code are the country):

```elixir
by_country =
  regions
  |> DF.mutate(country: substring(geo, 0, 2))
  |> DF.filter(country in ^~w(DE FR IT ES PL))

Vl.new(width: 600, height: 250, title: "GDP per inhabitant of the NUTS 2 regions (EU = 100)")
|> Vl.data_from_values(DF.select(by_country, ["country", "geo_label", "index"]))
|> Vl.mark(:tick, thickness: 2)
|> Vl.encode_field(:x, "index", type: :quantitative, title: "EU = 100")
|> Vl.encode_field(:y, "country", type: :nominal, title: nil)
|> Vl.encode(:tooltip, [[field: "geo_label"], [field: "index"]])
```
